 of\n\\(S_n\\) lies on at least one of the lines \\(M_1,\\dots ,M_n\\).\n\nThus the \\(n\\) sunny lines \\(M_1,\\dots ,M_n\\) give a configuration with\n\\(k=n\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  Completion of the proof\n\nWe have exhibited, for each integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\), a family of\n\\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the covering condition and containing exactly\n\\(k\\) sunny lines.  Therefore the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
